# howto: navigate fulcrum choices

a **fulcrum** is a point where a small choice tips a large outcome — a name that will spread, a shape many callers lean on, a boundary later work must respect. that weight is exactly why it must not halt the road.

the four moves:

1. **retain it in a list** — write it into the fulcrum inventory. do NOT stop the drive to raise it
2. **best-guess it, and offer to rework** — *"i chose X; if you prefer Y, it is a clean rework"*
3. **halt only when the rework is dirty** — and halt LAST, after every other question is addressed
4. **budget comes after approval** — never halt for lack of review rounds; the human tops up at the close

almost every fulcrum sits on rung 2. the block is the exception you earn only when rungs 1 and 2 are truly closed.

> do not halt the caravan at every fork to send a rider back. mark the fork on your map and drive on; at journey's end, show the map. 🪷

⇒ the mandate is `rule.always.defer-fulcrums-to-last`; the record is `rule.always.itemize-the-fulcrums-you-best-guess`.
